96369f62dcd93d8915230425190e2b6eafc7136aa36b7e4f01174c"},{"path":"modules/logging/nopencoder.go","sha256":"62290ad05cbb8aec63a79fad732680243ded8cace8e591f630ce6e74433d8a59"},{"path":"modules/metrics/adminmetrics.go","sha256":"33968cf21b4dedc907710a499cb3250278c9182ddb677bb5e21ae98d86235c5b"},{"path":"modules/metrics/metrics.go","sha256":"bea179181405d9977ea3844ce0843e41b18ec96359286a70a0d1c5ddd7b0c632"},{"path":"modules/metrics/metrics_test.go","sha256":"1318d06c8afad93adb3048991d7f96fb17d1f97b342daa11593d317a1e835774"},{"path":"modules/standard/imports.go","sha256":"207228f0ff1537602d5e1ba12e91d48928c2e91d808df0c418267c10137602d1"},{"path":"modules_test.go","sha256":"51b6e82ae353c8e469095189f109056a7cdaf9f7a5294c56b16eeb9615a5fc1d"}],"queries":[{"id":"repoqa-245fe284dc5b64e3361d","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: To measure the performance of a function that matches HTTP headers against a specified regular expression pattern.\n2. **Input**: A simulated HTTP request with a specific header and a regular expression pattern to match against this header.\n3. **Output**: There is no direct output from the benchmark itself, as it primarily measures the time and efficiency of the matching operation.\n4. **Procedure**: \n   - A regular expression pattern is defined and associated with a header field.\n   - The pattern is provisioned and validated for correctness.\n   - A simulated HTTP request is created with the specified header.\n   - A context and replacer are set up for the request to handle dynamic replacements based on the regular expression match.\n   - The matching function is executed repeatedly in a loop to measure its performance under continuous operation.\n","group":"caddyserver/caddy","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"modules/caddyhttp/matchers_test.go","grade":2,"spans":[[900,923]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-c0d793b90b91bf22262b","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: The function checks if a specific header value is present in the 'Vary' header of an HTTP response.\n2. **Input**: It takes an HTTP header and a target string as inputs.\n3. **Output**: It returns a boolean value indicating whether the target string is present in the 'Vary' header.\n4. **Procedure**: The function retrieves the values of the 'Vary' header, splits each value by commas to handle multiple entries, and checks each entry against the target string using a case-insensitive comparison. If the target string is found, it returns true; otherwise, it continues checking until all entries are exhausted and returns false if the target is not found.\n","group":"caddyserver/caddy","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"modules/caddyhttp/encode/encode.go","grade":2,"spans":[[378,388]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-39cf8eee87ff47f22e81","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: The function is designed to create a new library for expression matching, allowing the integration of custom matchers into expressions. It facilitates the use of specific data types and matching logic within the Common Expression Language (CEL) environment.\n2. **Input**: The function receives a macro name, a function name, a list of data types for the matcher, and a factory for creating matcher instances.\n3. **Output**: It returns a new CEL library configured with the specified macro and function, or an error if the provided data types or names are unsupported or cause conflicts.\n4. **Procedure**: \n   - The function first defines a request type.\n   - Based on the number and types of the input data types, it selects and configures a macro for expression parsing.\n   - It sets up an environment with the defined macro and a function that binds runtime logic for the matcher.\n   - It configures program options with custom decorators for additional runtime behavior.\n   - Finally, it constructs and returns a new CEL library using the environment and program options configured.\n","group":"caddyserver/caddy","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"modules/caddyhttp/celmatcher.go","grade":2,"spans":[[376,417]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-a9040bcc660c1e6df182","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: To determine if a specified file path should be considered hidden based on a list of patterns or specific file names.\n2. **Input**: A string representing a file path and a list of strings representing patterns or file names to hide.\n3. **Output**: A boolean value indicating whether the file path matches any of the hide patterns or specific file names.\n4. **Procedure**: \n   - If the list of hide patterns is empty, the function returns false.\n   - Converts the file path to an absolute path for accurate comparison.\n   - If a pattern does not contain a path separator, the function checks each component of the file path against the pattern.\n   - If a pattern contains a path separator, the function checks if the file path starts with the pattern, ensuring that it matches directories correctly.\n   - Additionally, the function performs a glob pattern matching to cover general cases where direct substring matching is insufficient.\n","group":"caddyserver/caddy","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"modules/caddyhttp/fileserver/staticfiles.go","grade":2,"spans":[[596,641]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-b944290e78009cd8f931","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: To retrieve the values of a specified header field from an HTTP header, with special handling for the \"Host\" header.\n2. **Input**: The function takes three parameters: an HTTP header object, a string representing the name of the header field to retrieve, and a string representing the host.\n3. **Output**: Returns a list of strings containing the values of the specified header field. If the field is \"Host\" and the host parameter is provided, it returns the host as the value.\n4. **Procedure**: The function first normalizes the header field name to its canonical form. If the field name is \"Host\" and a non-empty host value is provided, it returns the host value in a list. Otherwise, it retrieves the values associated with the header field name directly from the HTTP header object.\n","group":"caddyserver/caddy","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"modules/caddyhttp/matchers.go","grade":2,"spans":[[952,958]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-5faa9026fc833e13a071","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: To create a modified copy of an HTTP request for safe manipulation and forwarding to different destinations without altering the original request, ensuring thread safety and preventing data races.\n2. **Input**: A pointer to an HTTP request object.\n3. **Output**: A pointer to a new HTTP request object that is a semi-deep clone of the original.\n4. **Procedure**: \n   - A new HTTP request object is created.\n   - The new request is a shallow copy of the original request.\n   - The URL of the original request is deeply cloned, including the user information if present.\n   - The scheme and host of the URL are cleared to prevent unintended behavior in reverse proxy scenarios.\n   - Headers and trailers of the original request are deeply cloned to allow independent modification.\n","group":"caddyserver/caddy","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"modules/caddyhttp/reverseproxy/reverseproxy.go","grade":2,"spans":[[1154,1181]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-34cb20568988f722a4e1","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: To determine if two strings are equal, ignoring the case differences but only for ASCII characters.\n2. **Input**: Two strings.\n3. **Output**: A boolean value; `true` if the strings are equal ignoring case for ASCII characters, otherwise `false`.\n4. **Procedure**: The function first checks if the lengths of both strings are the same. If not, it returns `false`. If they are the same, it iterates through each character of the strings, converting each character to its lowercase ASCII equivalent and comparing them. If all corresponding characters match, it returns `true`; if any character does not match, it returns `false`.\n","group":"caddyserver/caddy","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"modules/caddyhttp/reverseproxy/ascii.go","grade":2,"spans":[[28,38]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-46b314f18354aa1c3b17","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: To generate a list of issuer configurations for certificate management, primarily used when no specific issuer details are provided.\n2. **Input**: A string representing the user's email address.\n3. **Output**: A list of issuer objects configured for certificate issuance, potentially including an email address if provided.\n4. **Procedure**: The function initializes a list with a default issuer object. If the provided email address is not empty, it appends another issuer object configured with a specific Certificate Authority and the provided email.\n","group":"caddyserver/caddy","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"modules/caddytls/automation.go","grade":2,"spans":[[397,406]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-4fa219c2a0481b4ee3f4","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: The function converts a list of challenge type strings into a list of challenge type constants.\n2. **Input**: A list of strings, each representing a type of challenge.\n3. **Output**: A list of constants, where each constant corresponds to a challenge type from the input list.\n4. **Procedure**: The function iterates over the input list of strings, converting each string into its corresponding challenge type constant, and collects these into a new list which is then returned.\n","group":"caddyserver/caddy","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"modules/caddypki/acmeserver/challenges.go","grade":2,"spans":[[71,77]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-bed67aaaab8a89ead713","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: The function is designed to generate a secure hash representation of a given string using a secret key. This is typically used for creating secure identifiers that can be used in cookies to maintain session integrity and security.\n2. **Input**: It takes two strings as inputs: a secret key and the data string that needs to be hashed.\n3. **Output**: Returns a hexadecimal string representation of the hashed data. If an error occurs during the hashing process, it returns an error alongside the hash.\n4. **Procedure**: The function initializes a new HMAC hasher using SHA-256 as the underlying hash function and the provided secret key. It then writes the data string to this hasher. After processing the data, it converts the resulting hash sum into a hexadecimal string format and returns this string.\n","group":"caddyserver/caddy","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"modules/caddyhttp/reverseproxy/selectionpolicies.go","grade":2,"spans":[[739,746]]}],"answerability":"answerable"}]}
